  "question": {
    "text": "The largest magnitude the electric field on the axis of a uniformly charged ring of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3&#160;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> from its centre. What is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>?&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>&#160;Take&#160;</mtext><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2.1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>axial&nbsp;</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>where,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo></math>radius of the ring,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo></math>distance of point from the centre.</p><p>For the maximum value,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>dh</mi></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mi>Qx</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>·</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>)</mo>